    "statementMarkdown": "A natural number $a$ is said to be contained in the natural number $b$ if it is possible to obtain $a$ by erasing some digits from $b$ (in their decimal representations). For example, 123 is contained in 901523, but not contained in 3412.\n\nDoes there exist an infinite set of natural numbers such that no number in the set is contained in any other number from the set?\n",
